	(gr_text "OPENAIO 8L HDI 1+6+1 (2026-10-15)  1.0 mm (0.997 with mask), 1 oz on all layers, ENIG\nStackup = OpenAIO-Whoop (NextPCB-confirmed, D123): 1080 / 1080 / core / 2116 / core / 1080 / 1080\nL1  F.Cu  parts (FC on top), high-side FET +BATT pours, phase pours\nL2  In1   GND plane (microvia target), /CSA+ corridor at the battery pad\nL3  In2   signals (Base), GND fill\nL4  In3   +BATT pour over the high-side FETs, +10V; Core links\nL5  In4   rails: +3V3, +3.3V, +4v5, +5V_USB, +10V; Core signals\nL6  In5   signals (Core) + +5V pour\nL7  In6   GND plane (microvia target)\nL8  B.Cu  parts (ESC side), low-side FET GND pours, phase pours\n\nVIAS while routing (edit form): ONE via per connection, 0.33/0.15 (net class default)\nV through via (F-B, or the layer pair), Option+Shift+V blind/buried on the active pair, Shift+V cycle pairs\n1-8 select layer L1-L8, D / G drag (router; via shoving is off)\nAfter routing, convert to the build form:\n  tools/via_types.py --buried-size 0.33/0.15   (stacks: microvia 0.25/0.10 on buried 0.33/0.15, through where F+B meet)\n  tools/via_min.py, tools/via_nudge.py, tools/drc_zero.py"
